        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 1089,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:37:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1074,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 1090,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154031,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 1090,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cellular blue naevus (87900/0)</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:37:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1075,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1091,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154032,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 1091,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Genital blue naevi are predominantly reported in the vaginal mucosa {589575}, but they can also occur in the cervix area, including the endocervix {689487}, and on the clitoris {27924655}. Vulvar lesions are rare.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:37:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1076,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1092,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154033,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 1092,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Blue naevus typically presents as an incidental small brown or black macular or papular lesion with a blue hue. Cellular blue naevus is larger and can become a pedunculated mass protruding into the vaginal cavity {21477275}. Multiple lesions have been described {10664947}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:37:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1077,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1093,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154034,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 1093,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Blue naevi are less common in the genital area than are other tumour types. In adults, vulvar melanocytic naevi are generally found in women in the reproductive age group {28778635; 25267379}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:37:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1078,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1094,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154035,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 1094,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:37:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1079,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1095,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154036,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 1095,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Blue naevi are thought to arise from precursors derived from dermal melanoblasts migrating to the skin during embryogenesis {24460190}. They are associated with activating mutations in <em>GNAQ</em>, <em>GNA11</em>, <em>PLCB4</em> (or less frequently in <em>CYSLTR2</em>) {19078957} or gene fusions in <em>PRKCA</em> or <em>PRKCB</em> {37474004}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:37:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1086,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1102,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154037,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 1102,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>, above.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:37:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1080,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1096,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154038,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 1096,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Blue naevi are located in the subepithelial tissue and form poorly circumscribed aggregates of small, darkly pigmented dendritic or spindled melanocytes associated with stromal fibroplasia. Involvement of adnexal adventitia or perivascular space is common. Melanophages can be present in some lesions. Cellular blue naevi are defined by the presence of often well-demarcated nodules composed of less-pigmented uniform spindled or oval melanocytes with vesicular nuclei and small nucleoli, arising in the context of otherwise unremarkable common blue naevus.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:37:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1081,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1097,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154039,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 276,
        "headingId": 1097,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T12:37:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1082,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1098,
    "contributions": [
